{
  "description": "Whether a channel's filter keeps a feed item. `filter` is a saved filter as stored in a device file; `item` holds only the fields the filter reads (absent means unknown). A filter field that is missing or holds an unrecognized value reads as its default; `regex` is applied only when it is a pattern built from phrases (one that shared/fixtures/phrases.json reads back into phrases); an invalid pattern, or a valid one that is not phrases, reads as no pattern, and a client writes `regex` as \"\" in its place the next time it saves that filter (it does not rewrite filters it is not saving). `topics` lists YouTube video category ids (shared/fixtures/feed-chips.json has the table); of them only the ids in the table count. With none of those the filter keeps every category; otherwise a video is kept only when its `categoryId` is one of them, so a video without a category or with one not in the table is dropped. A `topics` that is not an array, or holds anything but strings, reads as empty. Playlists skip this gate like the Shorts, live and duration ones.",
